 "amendments": [
  {
   "id": "A1",
   "before_judged_run": true,
   "text": "Records: the frozen definitions declare record times as decimals (round(0.1 k, 10)); the engine observes only accepted boundaries, the float products k * dt. Each record is taken at its own boundary int(round(t / dt)) * dt (a shift below 1e-16 s) and compared with the prediction at t (cell_replacement_qualification.at_dt)."
  },
  {
   "id": "A2",
   "before_judged_run": true,
   "text": "Pinning provenance: the dt study (qualification/dtstudy-02) ran at 15b5f7d, clean. The reference-term run (qualification/refterm-01) launched at 5fc5651 and records 15b5f7d, its HEAD when written; the one commit between them changes only the dt study's record mapping (A1), not the references. No engine output was compared with the frozen predictions before pinning."
  },
  {
   "id": "A3",
   "before_judged_run": true,
   "text": "Q5 estimator and cases. The full-size dry run on non-registered inputs (qualification/dryrun-01) gave registered-estimator orders 1.67 (W7 short-lag) and 2.95 (C9 donor short-lag). The order diagnosis on those inputs (qualification/q5-diagnosis, dt 4 to 0.25 ms) shows W7's successive-difference order rising 0.64, 1.67, 2.05 at h = 2, 1, 0.5 ms: second order, but asymptotic only below 1 ms. C9 donor's step error is at most 1e-9 V (no transient: a D copy among D neighbours), so its estimate is noise (2.2, 2.9, 4.5). C9 isolated short-lag gives 1.89, 2.06, 2.07. A3 therefore uses dt 2, 1, 0.5, 0.25 ms, the finest successive-difference ratio, and C9 isolated short-lag in place of C9 donor short-lag; the window is unchanged. Decided on non-registered inputs only; the registered cases were not run."
  }
 ],
